From 2ee6fca2bf57c7ef2934e46defbba12acc5b05c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:46:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add AI Vehicle Health Report for weekly inspections

Owner's pre-rental reference photos now appear as a real example when the
driver captures each inspection angle (previously just a generic diagram).

The AI report compares this week's photos against the driver's previous
inspection (falling back to the owner's reference photos on the first
inspection), and computes a health score, vehicle-identity verification,
photo quality rating, and flagged damage with an approximate location
overlay deterministically from Gemini's structured findings rather than
trusting a free-form score. Owners get a dedicated report screen with
Approve / Request Re-inspection / Flag Damage actions, a vehicle history
timeline, and a driver inspection record; approving awards +2 TrustScore
via a new database function.
